  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Kick out and dribble the lap",
  "description": "Two teams. Blue starts as the kicking team and stands by a goal; red spreads out on the pitch. Put out four cones as the corners of a big lap around the pitch, with a few spare balls next to the goal.\n\nThe first blue player kicks a ball out as far as they can, then takes a spare ball and dribbles it round the cones and back to the goal. Red collect the kicked ball and pass it into the goal. If it goes in while the blue player is dribbling between two cones, they are out and go back to the previous cone. A player standing at a cone is safe and can wait there until the next player has kicked. Swap roles after about five minutes.\n\nScoring: blue get a point for every player who gets home and three extra for a full lap on their own kick. Red get a point for every player they catch out. Feel free to invent more rules with the children. Variant: kick out on the volley, from the hands or after a throw from a teammate. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Kick the ball to where the opponents are not."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Keep the ball close to your feet round the cones so you don't lose it on the turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Red team: pass to whoever is nearest the goal instead of running with the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Look up before you leave a cone – can you reach the next one?"
    }
  ],
